    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d934">

                <pb facs="0727" n="611" sameAs="frus:frus1914/pg611"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 812.00/13570.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Vice Consul Silliman to
                        the Secretary of State.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Consulate</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Mexico City</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1914-10-22T18:00:00-06:36">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">October 22, 1914, 6 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Carranza has not heard further from Convention regarding Vera Cruz. Regardless of
                    Convention, his reply to American Government through Brazilian Minister, who on
                    October 8 communicated my telegram of 7th, 5 p.m., to Fabela, will be to the
                    effect that he considers it inexpedient for him to issue such a statement as the
                    Department desires. At the same time he says that no one will be molested on
                    account of service rendered Americans and no back duties or taxes will be
                    collected.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Silliman</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
